From: fxtec-pro1x-guix
Subject: [PATCH] Show the shortcuts bar when starting on the terminal layout

The shortcuts bar reads its shortcuts while the input surface's template
is built, before notify::num-shortcuts is connected, so that change is
never seen.  The deck's first child is the terminal layout: when the
first focused text field is a terminal (purpose 13), the visible child
never changes either, and the bar stays hidden for the whole session.
Seen in Sway on the Pro¹x, where all text input came from foot.
---
--- a/src/pos-input-surface.c
+++ b/src/pos-input-surface.c
@@ -2270,6 +2270,10 @@
   GAction *action;
 
   gtk_widget_init_template (GTK_WIDGET (self));
+  /* The shortcuts bar loads its shortcuts while the template is built,
+   * before notify::num-shortcuts is connected, and the deck starts on the
+   * terminal layout without a visible-child change: show the bar now. */
+  pos_input_surface_toggle_shortcuts_bar (self);
 
   self->bs_mode = POS_BACKSPACE_MODE_CHAR;
   self->style_manager = pos_style_manager_new ();
